[?2004l[?2004h>     "status": "ANSWERED",
[?2004lhe[?2004h>     "answer": "Important warnings and precautions associated with lopinavir and ritonavir include: the risk of serious adverse reactions due to drug interactions (since it is a CYP3A inhibitor); toxicity in preterm neonates due to ethanol and propylene glycol excipients (which can lead to cardiac toxicity, lactic acidosis, renal failure, CNS depression, and death); pancreatitis; hepatotoxicity; QT interval prolongation; PR interval prolongation; diabetes mellitus/hyperglycemia; immune reconstitution syndrome; lipid elevations; fat redistribution; and increased bleeding in hemophilia patients.",
